From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: emuTOS-MCD <darekadumon@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 13 Aug 2026 08:51:21 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 106/185] segacd: the diagnostic is Down again, not the default

It was briefly the default because a disc cost a CD-R and a boot that
reached a desktop instead of the test wasted one. Mode 1 kills that
reasoning: EmuTOS rides in the cartridge now and the image can be
rebuilt as often as anyone likes.

It was also the fault behind the white screen on hardware. Nothing
held ran the diagnostic, the diagnostic cleared the screen and then
blocked on Dfree, and the escape hatch needed a direction held for
thirty seconds. With the default gone, a CD boot with nothing held
reaches a full desktop again under gpgx -- verified by looking at the
frame this time, not by counting its colours.
---
 bios/segacd.c | 26 ++++++++++----------------
 1 file changed, 10 insertions(+), 16 deletions(-)

diff --git a/bios/segacd.c b/bios/segacd.c
index a1df7b9..69d1785 100644
--- a/bios/segacd.c
+++ b/bios/segacd.c
@@ -515,24 +515,18 @@ void segacd_cdd_init(void)
         segacd_diag = (UBYTE)((f & 4) ? 1 : 0);
         cd_lead = (f & 8) ? 2UL : 20UL;
         cd_selftest = (UBYTE)((f & 16) ? 1 : 0);
-        /* ...and by default, on this image.
+        /* The diagnostic is Down, and only Down.
          *
-         * The diagnostic is what this disc is burned to run, so a
-         * direction is the way out of it rather than the way in.
-         * Which direction registers at power-on has cost two runs
-         * already: Left never fired, and the only log this port has
-         * came off Up, which on this build is a different lever
-         * entirely. Any of Left, Up or Right skips to the desktop, so
-         * the escape does not rest on one button working.
+         * It was briefly the default, because a disc cost a CD-R and a
+         * boot that reached a desktop instead of the test wasted the
+         * disc. That reasoning is dead: a Mode 1 boot carries EmuTOS in
+         * the cartridge, so the image can be rebuilt as often as anyone
+         * likes and the ordinary boot should be the ordinary thing.
          *
-         * Set here rather than at the test in biosmain, so that a
-         * default run and a Down run are the same run. They were not
-         * when this was an || at the use site: segacd_diag also hands
-         * D: to the parked firmware two lines below, so "nothing held"
-         * quietly read the disc with a different driver and the two
-         * were not comparable. */
-        if (!(f & 0x3C))
-            segacd_diag = 1;
+         * It also could not work there. Nothing is held on a cart boot,
+         * so the default ran the diagnostic against an empty tray: the
+         * screen cleared and Dfree blocked on a drive with no disc in
+         * it, which looks exactly like a machine that never came up. */
         /* Right hands D: to the parked firmware. The diagnostic takes it
          * as well, without being asked, because holding Right and Down
          * together is a diagonal on a d-pad and the person holding it
